\title{some obstacles toward moser-tardos in catalytic logspace}

\p{\em{context.} this tree describes the obstacles towards resolving [[QP4OX]], specifically in the logspace regime.}

\p{initial obvious obstacle i thought was the recursion stack, but i don't that should be a problem, we don't have to recurse on the work tape. even though it might require careful handling of the auxilary tape, compression and recursive fix should be able to dovetailed, nice.}

\p{the more fundamental problem seems to be the root calls and the associated #{m\log m} space needed. one idea to overcome this might be another layer of compress-or-compute, where the root clauses are provided by the auxilary tape.}
